From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: cix: default acpi_scmi_en off so the clock bridge binds

device_deny_id_init() denies CIXHA010 -- the ACPI clock bridge -- whenever
acpi_scmi_en is true, and true is the default:

    if (acpi_scmi_en)
            acpi_deny_handler[DENY_SCMI_CLKS].ids = acpi_clks_deny_ids;  /* CIXHA010 */

The deny handler has no .attach, so acpi_bus_attach never runs the default
enumeration and no platform device is created for CIXHA010. Patch 0147
converted the bridge from an acpi_driver back to a platform_driver, which needs
exactly that device, and says so in its own commit message: "With SCMI enabled,
CIXHA010 is suppressed by the CIX ACPI scan handler, so users of that
configuration must retain the ACPI-driver variant or remove the deny policy
instead."

The result is that with the shipped default nothing provides clocks. MEASURED on
an Orion O6N booting the installer, read from a shell inside debian-installer:

    41 deferred probes matching "clock not found"
      CIXH2023:02  cix-pcie-phy: phy apb clock not found
      CIXH200B:00  cdns-i2c: input clock not found
    xhci never probes
    /proc/partitions empty, no /dev/sd*

so the USB medium the installer booted from is unreadable, and d-i reports "No
device for installation media was detected". The 7.0.12 kernel has no deny
mechanism at all, which is why the same ISO layout installed fine there and
regressed on 7.2.

Every successful 7.2 boot on this hardware has passed acpi_scmi_en=off on the
command line; the installed system's cmdline carries it. Making that the default
fixes the installer and every other boot path that does not know to pass it,
and acpi_scmi_en=on remains available for anyone who wants the SCMI-clocks
configuration together with the acpi_driver variant of the bridge.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]
Downstream fix to a downstream patch (0066/0147); neither exists upstream.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/soc/cix/acpi/cix-acpi-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/cix/acpi/cix-acpi-plat.c
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 
 static bool pcie_pnp_en = false;
 static bool usb_pnp_en = false;
-static bool acpi_scmi_en = true;
+static bool acpi_scmi_en = false;
 
 static int __init pcie_pnp_update(char *str)
 {
